    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"3\">Level 3 - Intermediate</span>\n    <span class=\"time\">55 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Build it yourself: 90 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Machine coding case</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Rank 38 of the LLD question list</span>\n  </div>\n  <h1>Rating System (Atlassian Code Design)</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">Atlassian's \"Customer Satisfaction\" code-design round: customers rate support agents out of 5; show every agent's average, highest first; then the interviewer adds ties, best agents per month and export formats, one tested step at a time. Razorpay asks a close cousin. You get the staged requirements, the class model, exact average comparison without floating point, a pluggable ranking policy, running Java, Python and C++14 code with a test per stage, and the follow-ups that decide the level.</p>\n"
  },
